	"notes": "The crypt rooms' music, one layer: A minor at 80 beats a minute, 32 bars (96 s) round, in two halves. The first is Am F Dm E, its chords held whole bars with a sevenths' colour, a wide room. The second (the owner's second listen, 2026-11-18: make it better) opens out to F C G Am and comes home through Am Dm F E and Dm Am E: the bells fall to a note or two a bar and low strings carry a slow tune, four bars with no drums, four with the brush alone, then the heartbeat again, so the loop has a breath in it and comes round half as often. Calm enough to hear for a whole run, under the effects and over the crypt's own air."
